WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.339 --> 00:00:04.000
[Music]

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.560
Before a new vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.920
is ever given to people, a lot of&nbsp;
testing is done in a laboratory.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.080
The next step is to test the vaccine in people in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.065
clinical trials.

00:00:13.172 --> 00:00:13.920
There are three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.680
phases of clinical trials to make&nbsp;
sure a vaccine is safe and effective:

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.120
During Phase I clinical trials, small groups of people get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.640
vaccine. Phase I clinical trials are used to&nbsp;
determine if the vaccine is generally safe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.520
if it works, if there are&nbsp;
any serious side effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.040
and what the best dose of the vaccine may be.
In Phase II clinical trials, scientists give the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.760
vaccine to a larger group of people, including&nbsp;
people who have characteristics (such as age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.720
and physical health) similar to those for whom the&nbsp;
new vaccine is intended. We use Phase II clinical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.920
trials to study short-term side effects and how&nbsp;
people’s immune systems respond to the vaccine.&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.720
In Phase III clinical trials, scientists give the&nbsp;
vaccine to thousands of people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.760
determine if the vaccine is safe and effective. In&nbsp;
particular, we use Phase III trials to determine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.680
how people who get the vaccine compare&nbsp;
with people who do not get the vaccine.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.560
Once the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)&nbsp;
approves a vaccine for use, the FDA continues to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.960
monitor the vaccine and its manufacturing&nbsp;
process to make sure that it remains safe.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.560
The United States also has extensive&nbsp;
vaccine monitoring systems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.680
where patients, health care professionals, vaccine&nbsp;
companies, and health insurance companies report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.830
side effects and other data to gather and&nbsp;
analyze information on the vaccine’s safety.

